      "summary": "In its first report the UN Panel of Experts called kidnapping for ransom 'one of the main sources of financing for gangs', counting 2,441 people kidnapped from January 2022 to June 2023. Ransoms in cases reported to it ranged from $7,000 to $500,000 for foreigners and prominent figures, against $3,000-$4,000 in earlier years, and captivity had lengthened to at least three weeks. Gangs hand hostages to other gangs for a 'commission' or 'sell' them, and some kidnappers wear police uniforms. The panel also described migrant smuggling from Port-de-Paix, where boats built for $25,000-$50,000 to hold about 20 people carry 80 to 100 at $1,000-$3,000 each.",
