      "title": "UN experts: opaque baby-eel trade launders money, pays gangs",
      "summary": "The UN Panel of Experts reported that Haiti's export of elvers (baby eels) is controlled by about 20 permit holders answering to one 'businessman and influential politician'. Exporters earn $4,000-5,000 a kilogram for eels bought from fishers at $0.50-1.50; the Panel calculated a profit of about $1.07 million on a single 250 kg consignment. 400 Mawozo takes $200-500 per tank on the road, and exporters' agents pay 400 Mawozo and Gran Grif $2,000-3,000 a week to protect collection points.",
